-- Divisibility of the chain of theta lifts at each prime: integrality of
-- B_μ at good primes, the valuation of B_μ at small non-split primes, the
-- size of all conjugates of the untwisted chain, and the chain divisible
-- by the predicted power of p on a submodule of small index.
-- Source: grh-compact/src/New/Columns/LocalStatement.lean ("Divisibility
-- of the chain of theta lifts at each prime. ... Short columns span, and
-- the size of all conjugates of the chain."; Data.liftLoss,
-- Data.IsGoodDatum.gaugeLe_one, gaugeLe_collisionSum,
-- gaugeLe_pow_jetCeil_smul, Data.weylNormSq_Bmu_le,
-- Data.exists_indexDvd_Bmu_divisible).
-- Encoding. The chain B_μ, IsGoodDatum and the split Hecke operators are
-- FORWARD (GRH.Proof.Columns.TwistedHeckeType); the level prime is L.N.
-- The O_ι-submodule S of the source is a set of columns with
-- ColumnOSubmodule. Not stated here: the Hecke-transfer steps
-- (exists_hecke_transfer, IsGoodDatum.mem_raises,
-- exists_move_markOperator, gaugeLe_markOperator_pow,
-- IsMarked.hasType_prod_markOperator_pow, gaugeLe_Bmu_of_isMarked), which
-- need the chains of lift kernels, the Hecke operators of a marked set in
-- a chosen order and their passage through the lifts.
-- Part of the GRH blueprint (layer 5, the argument).
